  abstract  = "BACKGROUND: The U.K. 100,000 Genomes Project is in the process
               of investigating the role of genome sequencing in patients with
               undiagnosed rare diseases after usual care and the alignment of
               this research with health care implementation in the U.K.
               National Health Service. Other parts of this project focus on
               patients with cancer and infection. METHODS: We conducted a
               pilot study involving 4660 participants from 2183 families,
