               disparities in precision medicine. By whole-genome sequencing of
               4,810 Singapore Chinese, Malays, and Indians, we found 98.3
               million SNPs and small insertions or deletions, over half of
               which are novel. Population structure analysis demonstrated
               great representation of Asian genetic diversity by three
               ethnicities in Singapore and revealed a Malay-related novel
               ancestry component. Furthermore, demographic inference suggested
               that Malays split from Chinese 24,800 years ago and experienced
               significant admixture with East Asians 1,700 years ago,
